30a8ad-6905-4b93-8749-50784fe9421c", "type": "concept", "title": "Subordination and coordination"}], "description": "This subtopic focuses on the architecture of Spanish sentences."}, {"id": "7a995174-b566-4b06-8f8e-977b107b10fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Syntactic phenomena in Spanish", "children": [{"id": "14d33f37-f3b4-418a-bbed-f0df79e0bae4", "type": "concept", "title": "Null subjects"}, {"id": "d7945d2c-4d08-41ef-9e50-94d9de8ee117", "type": "concept", "title": "Clitic placement"}, {"id": "d4459be3-646b-434f-a96e-1ca87a202fa7", "type": "concept", "title": "Differential object marking"}, {"id": "fae03b98-7c00-46b9-98cf-79fd03af7254", "type": "concept", "title": "Subjunctive environments"}], "description": "Students analyze patterns that are central to Spanish grammar."}]}, {"id": "71fe5f1c-7e45-4c92-9489-bbff794210d9", "type": "topic", "title": "Semantics, Pragmatics, and Discourse", "description": "Students study how meaning is encoded, inferred, negotiated, and organized across words, sentences, conversations, and texts.", "children": [{"id": "eb14d0e6-8104-4c89-a64f-3098579654ee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lexical and compositional meaning", "children": [{"id": "b5165427-596a-47a1-9a2b-377bf7f93d1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Sense and reference"}, {"id": "64fb5dfb-5be2-4899-857b-4dc39fc1221d", "type": "concept", "title": "Polysemy"}, {"id": "10be94f8-6ad5-4d25-9386-e8758f0fb86d", "type": "concept", "title": "Entailment"}, {"id": "62458b44-0928-4870-ad5f-529622d712a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Aspectual meaning"}], "description": "This subtopic covers how words and sentence structures create meaning."}, {"id": "99940650-a13d-44b8-8325-81dbfc118c29", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pragmatic interpretation", "children": [{"id": "740237c3-60c3-413d-a5e8-9a825aae7658", "type": "concept", "title": "Implicature"}, {"id": "0c021e3f-b180-4a79-b6b6-b8a7a0e76ed9", "type": "concept", "title": "Speech acts"}, {"id": "2a140cf0-cc95-4ec3-aacf-1caa59a7a054", "type": "concept", "title": "Politeness"}, {"id": "1b896f37-cc65-4327-961c-a102d0e483e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Deixis"}], "description": "Students learn how context changes what an utterance communicates."}, {"id": "b77932e4-d4e9-4962-92e4-7f52cee05e3f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Discourse organization", "children": [{"id": "f11b4439-0e18-4434-9f0e-8a641dc9c544", "type": "concept", "title": "Topic and focus"}, {"id": "b44d61bc-43d5-4e55-9d69-2c8408aa41d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Discourse markers"}, {"id": "f07445a1-c309-4ab3-b307-58ea92cd71bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Information structure"}, {"id": "f1b16463-7256-442e-8f14-e1db54f7bf9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative sequencing"}], "description": "Students examine how Spanish speakers manage coherence across larger stretches of language."}]}, {"id": "2f15a524-241f-4cf9-9436-5f208f782876", "type": "topic", "title": "Historical Development of Spanish", "description": "This topic traces Spanish from Latin through medieval, early modern, colonial, and contemporary stages.", "children": [{"id": "314a8841-4c0e-48ff-96c0-c83e55f7437f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "From Latin to Romance", "children": [{"id": "c982dea6-43b6-4fb5-9b4e-650c94003d0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Vulgar Latin"}, {"id": "893062ba-c3c4-4d8a-b799-7c45a913d8c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Sound change"}, {"id": "e76cbca7-094e-46e7-8503-0b7af40cf6d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Morphosyntactic change"}, {"id": "1bacaf5c-bd95-4410-a94b-26b253f5435b", "type": "concept", "title": "Early Romance varieties"}], "description": "Students learn the broad historical processes that produced Spanish."}, {"id": "63e1e4d8-bcf1-4938-8c08-90be69010143", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Medieval and early modern Spanish", "children": [{"id": "94fa789e-8745-46ed-a4fe-f115dc4fc4cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Old Spanish"}, {"id": "81286107-a57a-42b2-8f11-7257370f362d", "type": "concept", "title": "Alfonso X and written norms"}, {"id": "8b8bfd4f-f5fb-47a0-8f00-85a3a89f2604", "type": "concept", "title": "Printing and standardization"}, {"id": "d69fcb8b-05ba-459f-8eff-6cd719ecf4ee", "type": "concept", "title": "The role of grammar and dictionaries"}], "description": "This subtopic connects language history to writing, standardization, and institutions."}, {"id": "1934ec8d-1a8a-4e55-9a08-cf89dff59a4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global expansion and change", "children": [{"id": "b2bc5be8-70d2-49a5-b7ba-77b6c72b12b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Colonial Spanish"}, {"id": "34a92833-c1b8-43bb-bb76-8d9818117e34", "type": "concept", "title": "American varieties"}, {"id": "8f23433d-cd10-4abd-a8a5-3fa2bbbb742f", "type": "concept", "title": "Language academies"}, {"id": "8c829a0c-19d1-4635-8978-919edc53c006", "type": "concept", "title": "Contemporary global Spanish"}], "description": "Students examine how Spanish changed through empire, migration, and contact."}]}, {"id": "f8785c8a-080f-4a98-8717-83bba0ad49c6", "type": "topic", "title": "Dialectology and Regional Variation", "description": "This added topic makes the variation unit more world-class by treating Spanish as a pluricentric language with regional systems rather than a single standard.", "children": [{"id": "c7e9bd25-b49d-4a15-a8f3-90cd6cb23434", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mapping Spanish varieties", "children": [{"id": "22d86e55-c1a9-42ed-8a11-ce24df019738", "type": "concept", "title": "Peninsular varieties"}, {"id": "be8683f5-8cde-42c4-88e8-b597108fa4ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Caribbean Spanish"}, {"id": "bf96d986-af30-4bcb-ba59-e29d16c4aaac", "type": "concept", "title": "Mexican and Central American Spanish"}, {"id": "6417f6b0-3d82-400a-ab0b-f54a8ce0ac23", "type": "concept", "title": "Andean, Rioplatense, and Chilean Spanish"}], "description": "Students compare major regional patterns across the Spanish-speaking world."}, {"id": "3356d6ff-0b55-4110-a917-973f23284ff7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regional features", "childr