rent kinds of questions about Spanish."}, {"id": "7debce91-bd50-4e2e-8b3c-1003842f70b2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Linguistic evidence", "children": [{"id": "0d14309e-128e-463f-aa2d-34c037b3938c", "type": "concept", "title": "Speaker judgments"}, {"id": "29971ffd-7f49-4fc4-b28a-2765a987aa45", "type": "concept", "title": "Corpus examples"}, {"id": "f720e099-b41b-4737-9209-d3252b26e43c", "type": "concept", "title": "Acoustic and articulatory data"}, {"id": "8d27e30b-3145-44ce-8dfb-04fd78a8f1be", "type": "concept", "title": "Sociolinguistic interviews"}], "description": "Students learn what counts as evidence in linguistic analysis."}]}, {"id": "57caa34e-7d68-4469-bdf6-8afa5a869391", "type": "topic", "title": "Phonetics, Phonology, and Sound Patterns", "description": "Students examine how Spanish sounds are produced, perceived, patterned, and varied across speakers and regions.", "children": [{"id": "09c76849-cb35-4747-9bd7-897846894381", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Articulatory phonetics", "children": [{"id": "6985903a-2168-4451-babd-ce627a0a6118", "type": "concept", "title": "Place and manner of articulation"}, {"id": "3cfbd9b1-37b2-4e56-9b3d-8e626f8fd37c", "type": "concept", "title": "Voicing"}, {"id": "c546b7d7-0385-4d74-8086-61bcfe319ea1", "type": "concept", "title": "Vowel system"}, {"id": "e98239ee-06b4-4803-a053-b2620473045c", "type": "concept", "title": "IPA transcription"}], "description": "Students learn how the vocal tract produces Spanish consonants and vowels."}, {"id": "65cf53eb-3b25-4bfd-994c-21785b961b4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Phonological patterns", "children": [{"id": "4d3ce64b-1b8e-4518-a03d-3f01bb957080", "type": "concept", "title": "Phonemes and allophones"}, {"id": "832abc58-aa6e-49c1-8de9-625674f77939", "type": "concept", "title": "Syllable structure"}, {"id": "ea6956a9-876e-42b3-81b6-22453caeca4c", "type": "concept", "title": "Stress and intonation"}, {"id": "32efa191-81aa-4b79-b11b-7e559fe9858b", "type": "concept", "title": "Assimilation and weakening"}], "description": "This subtopic moves from individual sounds to sound systems and rules."}, {"id": "40a84911-9996-492b-a686-f389f60e2474", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spanish sound variation", "children": [{"id": "86a5806b-a4e7-4a02-8bab-89bbee7169ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Seseo and ceceo"}, {"id": "48208668-6491-407e-8b7d-23fc88c27a96", "type": "concept", "title": "Yeísmo"}, {"id": "ca97a9f0-ae77-48d6-8561-5ce54067f0b1", "type": "concept", "title": "S-aspiration and deletion"}, {"id": "62c4a286-a045-4ebc-a2ca-51f5bd4d8a85", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhotics and lateral variation"}], "description": "Students connect sound patterns to geography, identity, register, and contact."}]}, {"id": "bd417339-c347-4b1d-948b-c939c06eebf9", "type": "topic", "title": "Morphology and Word Formation", "description": "Morphology shows how Spanish builds words and encodes grammatical meaning through roots, stems, affixes, and inflection.", "children": [{"id": "132ff5d3-ee81-49b3-8d03-87f40a135fcc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inflectional morphology", "children": [{"id": "77777c8e-18bc-48df-be36-e37798b24eaf", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender and number"}, {"id": "84ce73e0-e03e-4c77-aed6-3bd91cc02207", "type": "concept", "title": "Person and agreement"}, {"id": "8184a3fe-cacb-4bcd-8f57-78dfa1184329", "type": "concept", "title": "Tense, aspect, and mood"}, {"id": "643ff460-0da1-4300-8658-e97532808ced", "type": "concept", "title": "Clitics and pronouns"}], "description": "Students learn how Spanish marks grammatical categories inside words."}, {"id": "611d9f74-24bd-4fbd-bbbb-b0b2de3bb95b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Derivational morphology", "children": [{"id": "0e18b66b-0230-460a-a3a7-502bb62add77", "type": "concept", "title": "Prefixes"}, {"id": "b67d9d5a-1cb6-453a-8f26-6f9708bb8e06", "type": "concept", "title": "Suffixes"}, {"id": "9efdc638-8430-4a85-9740-27c217e7c9ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominalization"}, {"id": "065235fa-9e4